Z||000000||Galen||08-16-2001||02:40 AM||||How do you decide which one you will drive? or do you go like, yup this one today.. then this one tomorrow..<P>I can just imagine seeing one of ya'll standing in ya yard thinking.. "Which one today?"<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"With one drop of blood he realized his own mortallity, it was then he saw the true face of God. For he is not someone watching down on us, but he is in us." - Galen 2001</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||08-16-2001||03:52 AM||||Hrm, lessee, which one should I drive?<P>"Monday" "Tuesday" Wendsday" "Thursday" "Friday" "Saturday" or "Sunday?"<P>If I got another, it'd have to be "Leap Day!"<P>(just kidding, I drive the one of my two cars that's running....)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-16-2001||04:06 AM||||Dunno, I dont own multiple Fieros....oh, wait...........................  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>To answer your question, usually the one to drive is the one giving you the least probs that day!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> In all honesty, I actually only drive a couple of mine. The rest either dont run quite right, or dont run at all.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RRobinson||08-16-2001||09:10 AM||||Depends how hot it is....<P>Mild = No air/no sunroof ok<BR>Hot = No air/sunroof ok<BR>Damn hot = air/sunroof ok<BR>Super damn hot = air/no sunroof ok<P>That's how I pick. Also, dead batterys and low tires usually help me pick a fiero.<P>RR<BR>2-88 GTs<BR>2-87 GTs<BR>87 SE V6<BR>86 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
Z||000004||Springtyme||08-16-2001||09:17 AM||||Eric used to have two. I'd drive his red stick one and he'd drive his baby (the black one he's working on and has been for the past 4 years) but sometimes he'd take the red one cause he insisted that it ran better than his black one (I Beg to differ) I guess it just decides which Fiero you're in the mood to drive. =)<P>------------------<BR>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||08-16-2001||09:29 AM||||I own 5. Only one is road worthy. Pretty easy decision.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> If ever I build one with a V8, the decision will most likely be based on how far I have to go and how much gas in in each tank!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Elvira||08-16-2001||09:30 AM||||Well, right now only one of our 4 (soon to be 5 1/2) is drivable and that is Chester's Black 86GT showcar.  My Blue 87GT is patiently waiting for the 3.1 to go in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">(hopefully in the next couple of weeks!), our other 86Black GT has now become our V8 conversion donor, our 86 coupe with t-tops just needs brakes and fluids changed (and t-top seals) and then we have the 4seater that we are picking up next weekend.  With only one running it is kind of easy to pick, but lookout when they are all going!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||7
